// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// The mirror of neg-domain-measure-no-canonical-unit.pure: a Measure has EXACTLY one
// canonical unit, so marking a second with '*' is as wrong as marking none.
//
// The pair is deliberate. A rewrite that treats '*' as a per-unit boolean flag -- the
// obvious reading, since it is written on the unit -- gets both of these wrong in opposite
// directions: zero canonical units becomes a measure with no base, two becomes a measure
// whose conversion functions disagree about what they convert to. Neither is a parse error
// for that implementation, and neither ever fails loudly.
###Pure
Measure fixture::neg::TwoCanonical
{
   *Gram: x -> $x;
   *Kilogram: x -> $x * 1000;
}
